{% comment %}
  Mirrors build.py's header(). Nav comes from a real Shopify menu (Admin →
  Navigation) via the menu setting below, rather than hardcoded links, so
  adding a page doesn't require a Liquid edit — set the default to whichever
  menu holds The range / Bundles / The idea / Start.

  section.settings.menu.links[*].active is Shopify's own current-page flag;
  no equivalent yet exists here for "an ancestor section is active" (the
  data-section state the GitHub Pages nav uses for product pages inside The
  range) — Shopify menus don't expose a parent/section relationship the way
  a flat NAV list in Python could. Worth a follow-up if that state matters
  enough to replicate; for now every non-active link renders identically.
{% endcomment %}
<header class="site-header">
  <div class="wrap site-header__inner">
    {% render 'lockup' %}
    <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
      {%- for link in section.settings.menu.links -%}
        <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title }}</a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </nav>
    {% render 'cart-toggle' %}
  </div>
</header>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Header",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "link_list", "id": "menu", "label": "Primary navigation", "default": "main-menu" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
